    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a2">

                <pb facs="0241" n="133" xml:id="pg133"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 173.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral Magnaghi
                        to Capt. Picking.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that following the suggestions expressed by the
                    superior commanders of all naval forces present in Rio de Janeiro, I sent an
                    officer to ask the captain of the port to indicate the space assigned for the
                    anchorage of merchant and war vessels. The reply was made verbally but
                    officially, and a line was traced on the plan of the bay fixing the limit of the
                    safe anchorage for all ships. Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. B. Magnaghi.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
